.Dd November 5, 2026
.Dt ELF_LINK_PLAN_SET_KEEP_GROUPS 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm elf_link_plan_set_keep_groups
.Nd keep the inputs' section groups in a link's output
.Sh LIBRARY
libelfobj
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In elfobj.h
.Ft elf_err_t
.Fn elf_link_plan_set_keep_groups "elf_link_plan_t *plan" "int enable"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
With
.Fa enable
nonzero, a link through
.Fa plan
keeps the section groups
.Pq Dv SHT_GROUP
of its inputs, as GNU ld does for relocatable output
.Pq Fl r .
Each input group is one of the output's, under the same signature and
flags.
Its members go to output sections of their own, still marked
.Dv SHF_GROUP ,
which no section of another group or of none joins; their relocation
sections are members too.
A COMDAT group of a signature already seen is left out with its members,
whether or not groups are kept.
A group's signature is the output's symbol of that name; a local symbol
an input defines in the group's section, as GNU as makes one for a
signature nothing else names, is kept in the output group's section.
.Pp
Off by default: the groups are not kept, and their members go into the
output as other sections do.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Returns
.Dv ELF_OK
on success, otherwise
.Dv ELF_ERR_STATE
for a NULL
.Fa plan .
.Sh EXAMPLES
Keep the groups, as a relocatable link does.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
#include <elfobj.h>

int
main(void)
{
    elf_link_plan_t *plan = elf_link_plan_create();

    elf_link_plan_set_keep_groups(plan, 1);
    elf_link_plan_destroy(plan);
    return 0;
}
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr elf_link 3 ,
